<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="024" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>spaarke_complete_decision app-only write tool</title>
    <phase>B MCP host and tools</phase>
    <gate>after 014, 017 and 021</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; new tool class and data-mutation tests (.cs)</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Thin adapter over the unchanged commit entry (IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync → DecisionCommitService); every invariant is already server-side and tested</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>F</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds only its own tool and test files; shares no file with 022, 023 or 030</parallel-reason>
    <deps>014, 017, 021</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement spaarke_complete_decision, the only write tool: app-only, not readOnly, input signalId and a DecisionReview with the same contract as POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision, calling IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync and nothing else, with one MCP test proving a billing Signal returns the mapped decided_in_invoice_review refusal and writes nothing.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in idempotent write APIs and MCP tool annotations.</role>
  <goal>The tool is listed app-only with readOnlyHint false; one call writes one Decision Record and closes the Signal; replays return the first outcome; the refusal negatives hold; no second billing check exists.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-08, FR-15 (server half), NFR-06; design §7.1 and §10; ontology condition 2. O-14: no model-callable complete tool in v1.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/data-mutation/Mcp/CompleteDecisionToolTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCapability.Commit.cs (from 014)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/data-mutation/Signals/DecisionCommitServiceTests.InvoiceReview.cs (billing fixture shapes)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs (DecisionReview binding and JSON options)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="014" status="pending">IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync</dependency>
      <dependency task="017" status="pending">DecisionResultMapper</dependency>
      <dependency task="021" status="pending">A10 auth and per-tool policies</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">spaarke_complete_decision is app-only (never model-visible), readOnlyHint false, destructiveHint false, idempotentHint true, named per the naming note, with a title and a 'use for / not for' description of at most 1,024 characters.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">This task adds no billing-refusal check of its own: D-207 (ontology.decision.decided_in_invoice_review) applies only through DecisionCommitService's existing (1c-billing) step (DecisionCommitService.cs:975-996).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">The tool calls only IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync with the DecisionReview deserialised by the same contract and JSON options as POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision; it adds no validation, rights check or write of its own, and relies on no host confirmation prompt (NFR-06).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Every tool this task adds reads the request HttpContext from IHttpContextAccessor and passes it (or its User) to the decision capability. A null HttpContext or an unauthenticated caller returns an isError result with UserContextRequired (DATAVERSE_USER_CONTEXT_REQUIRED) before any capability call, and nothing falls back to an app-only client (FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, option C; ADR-002 WP-6 fail closed). No ICallerContext or other caller holder is introduced.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Every domain failure from a tool added by this task is returned as an isError tool result produced by DecisionResultMapper.ToToolError → Api/Mcp/McpToolResults (reasonCode plus a fix-the-call message); no domain failure is returned as a transport error or exception.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">Tools added by this task inject only the decision capability, IDecisionLookupSearch and Api/Mcp helpers: no AI-internal type (Services/Ai/**, IChatClient, playbook services).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">File ownership for parallel safety: this task adds only its own files under Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/ and its own test files; tools are discovered per area by attribute (set up in 020), so no shared registration file is edited.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">Every log statement or telemetry property this task adds records identifiers, sizes, timings and outcome/reason codes only: no bearer token, claim value, record text or tool argument (NFR-05).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The `spaarke_complete_decision` error result for a Failed commit carries the D-17 `Partial` payload from task 014 (`DecisionToolError.Partial`) in its structured content, so the host and the widget can tell the user which writes landed and whether a resend with the same review id resumes the decision (ontology, 2026-11-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-10">One caller per call (013 known limit, confirmed by ontology review, 2026-11-07). The capability's guard checks the `HttpContext` passed in, while `SignalCoreRecordAccess`, `IDataverseUserClient` and the plan stamp run as the ambient request's caller. This tool passes exactly `IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext`, never a constructed or cached `HttpContext`. A test pins that the tool's call uses the same instance as `IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run `bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master` (blocking Tier 1 'Format (changed C# files)'; fix with `dotnet format whitespace . --folder --include &lt;file&gt;`). CS0618 (obsolete API) is a build error since master 9456083c78: migrate the call or escalate, never suppress it in Directory.Build.props, NoWarn or a file-wide pragma.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08">The tool returns the commit result unchanged. `DecisionCommitResult.Warnings` (DecisionCommitService.cs ~L191; D-216, ontology task 176) and each step's `Warning` (`DecisionActionOutcome` / `DecisionCommitStep`, for example `inquiry_email_not_archived`) must reach structuredContent. Do not slim, re-project or drop them.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-002-thin-plugins.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-015-ai-data-governance.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/pre-pipeline-context.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Implement CompleteDecisionTool: input signalId + DecisionReview (same contract as the REST route); read the HttpContext from IHttpContextAccessor (null or unauthenticated → isError UserContextRequired) and call IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync with it; return the commit result unchanged as structuredContent (including `warnings[]` and each step's `warning`) or failures through McpToolResults.</step>
    <step order="2">Write data-mutation tests for the acceptance criteria, reusing #2580's billing fixture shapes for the one billing test.</step>
    <step order="3">Run the suites (including Task174_* and 011's commit baselines); measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="5">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any criterion seems to need logic in the tool beyond calling the capability (a check, a retry, a write), STOP and escalate: DecisionCommitService is the single owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision (DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs) over DecisionCommitService.</existing>
    <extension>It is the extension: a thin adapter over IDecisionCapability.CommitAsync, the same entry the REST route uses.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A Work Item cannot be resolved in Copilot or Cowork, so the v1 goal (O-2) and success criteria 2 and 3 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Mcp/LegalOperations/Decisions/CompleteDecisionTool.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/Mcp/CompleteDecisionToolTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">tools/list shows spaarke_complete_decision with app-only visibility and readOnlyHint false; it is absent from the model-visible tool set.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">One completion writes one Decision Record and closes the Signal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The same reviewId sent twice returns the first outcome and writes nothing new.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a commit with no prior plan read on a system-closed Signal returns isError with `signal_not_open` and writes nothing. A missing stamp means "review starts now" (ISS-004 ruling, 2026-11-07). If the tool also requires the plan tool to have run first, that requirement is a usability guard, not the security check.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller without Write on a subject returns isError ontology.decision.not_authorized and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a billing Signal (subject sprk_invoice or sprk_billingevent) returns isError reasonCode ontology.decision.decided_in_invoice_review, writes nothing and does not call the rights probe (the one MCP billing test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: with no HttpContext (accessor null) or an unauthenticated caller, the tool returns an isError result with UserContextRequired and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A because value in the DecisionReview appears on the written Decision Record (FR-15 server half).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">structuredContent carries `DecisionCommitResult` unchanged, including `warnings[]` and each step's `warning`. Test: a budget-inquiry commit whose archival fails returns success with `warnings` containing `inquiry_email_not_archived`, matching REST for the same input.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep shows no billing check, IsBillingSubject call or rights check under Api/Mcp/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An MCP-level test shows that a Failed commit returns `isError` with structuredContent containing `landed`, `possiblyLanded` and `resumable`, matching REST for the same failure.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>FR-08 and ontology condition 2. The widget sends this only from the wizard's explicit Confirm (032).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
